## Completion report: fix-minion-town-pr180-ocap-key-audit-20261017

All three steps are done. The audit found no identity-shaped secret that a guest or caplet can reach, so #180's code is unchanged. I regrouped its commits and recorded the ruling in §7 through a new design PR.

**1. Audit.** I applied the identity-vs-object test to every secret in the control plane, including rotation, the `/hello` check, open-by-id and the mint-cap paths.

| Secret | What it designates | Can a guest reach it? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Capability-URL token | One partition at one attenuation; each attenuation has its own live-URL cap | Yes, as the minted URL |
| Retention key (`open`) | One partition, read+write; `open` checks nothing else, not even the owner | Yes, as `create`'s result; it is kept inside the guest's `open` formula |
| Facet key (`mint`/`revoke`) | One partition at one attenuation; a read facet can revoke only read URLs | No, it is closed over inside the partition object |
| Owner credential (`create`) | One owner's partition allocator, capped by quota; it reaches no existing partition | No, it sits in the caplet formula the host holds |
| `/hello` proof | Nothing; it only lets the caller tell the real listener from a squatter, and is bound to the port | It is only ever an answer |
| Root secret | Master authority; owner credentials and facet keys derive from it | No; only the `minion-git-remote` and `minion-mcp` processes load it, never the Endo daemon or any formula |

Rotating the root secret strands no partition: stale owner credentials stop working, and `open` re-derives facet keys under the current secret.

Two things for the maintainer, both sent to the inbox:
- **Owner credential (needs a ruling):** it is derived from the owner's name and shared by all of that owner's guests. I classed it as designating one object, because it only allows `create` on that owner's allocator. A leaked copy can at worst use up the owner's partition quota. If the maintainer reads it as identity-shaped, the fix is small: key it per guest or per caplet instead of per owner.
- **Read facet key (left alone):** all read-only copies of one partition share a single read key. Holders of different read copies can therefore revoke each other's read URLs and draw on one mint budget. I made no change, since the job said no further hardening.

